1.  SCOPE AND BACKGROUND

    The Prebuilt Libraries are the static archives that the service
    binaries of this project link against: libcode.a is linked into
    rolling_helper, libmtk_<project>_<oem>_<version>.a supplies the
    platform-specific helper layer, and the two librolling_*_service_*.a
    archives carry the config and flash service implementations.

    They are compiled from internal sources that are not published in this
    repository.  That repository publishes only the service entry points
    (rolling_config_main.c, rolling_flash_main.c, rolling_helper_main.c),
    the headers and the D-Bus / systemd / udev integration; the translation
    units compiled into these archives (rolling_config_parse.c,
    rolling_flash_update.c, rolling_helper_adapter.c and others -- 24 in total) are
    not part of it.

    The Prebuilt Libraries therefore cannot be rebuilt from the published
    sources, and they are NOT covered by the GNU Lesser General Public
    License version 2.1 that applies to the published source code (see the
    LICENSE file in the top-level directory, SECTION A).  Redistribution in
    binary form is granted by the copyright holder under this license.  The
    repository-level LICENSE file states the same grant in its SECTION B;
    this file is the self-contained copy that travels with the archives.


